  "summary": "Updates the \"How to Upgrade\" documentation to instruct users to copy both the `bin/` and `libexec/` directories when installing new releases. This ensures the multiprocess wrapper and its corresponding binaries are upgraded together.",
  "problem": "Users manually upgrading Bitcoin Core on Linux by copying only `bitcoind` or `bitcoin-qt` leave the multiprocess helper binaries in `libexec/` outdated, causing issues when using the `bitcoin` wrapper executable introduced in #31375.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: \"Since #31375, Linux installs ship a bitcoin wrapper in bin/ that dispatches to multiprocess binaries in libexec/. Copying only bitcoind/bitcoin-qt leaves those stale.\"",
    "Resolves open issue #36431: 'doc: \"How to Upgrade\" release notes section is outdated since the `bitcoin` wrapper executable'"
